-- title:
--   Principal-level spherical flat test functions approximate cuspidal L² classes
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, let $\alpha,\beta\in\mathbb{R}$ and let $\Phi_0\subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ satisfy `IsSlabFundamentalDomain`: $0<\alpha<\beta$, every $g\in\Phi_0$ has idele norm of $\det g$ in $[\alpha,\beta]$, and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ acting on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ for the adelic Haar measure restricted to that slab. Let $\sigma\in\mathbb{R}$ and let $\xi$ be a character of the full group of idele units with $\|\xi(z)\|=\|z\|^{\sigma}$, let $N\neq 0$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_F$, and let `tys` be a family assigning to each infinite place $w$ finitely many finite-dimensional representations of the row-isometry subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F_w)$. Let $x:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to\mathbb{C}$ be a continuous smooth cuspidal automorphic member for the pins attached to $\Phi_0$ with level-one family and character $\xi$, right invariant under the principal congruence subgroup $K(N)$ intersected with the kernel of the archimedean projection, and lying in the type cut submodule of `tys`. Then for every $\varepsilon>0$ there is $f:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to\mathbb{C}$ which is a factorizable test function (a smooth compactly supported archimedean factor times a locally constant compactly supported finite factor), which is level-spherical of type `tys` for that same principal level group, namely $f(g)=f_\infty(g_\infty)$ times the indicator of the level group at $g_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $f_\infty$ an archimedean test factor, bi-finite for `tys` and invariant under conjugation by the archimedean row isometries, and which is flat-symmetric, $f(y)=\overline{f(y^{-1})}\,\|\det y\|^{-\sigma}$; moreover the right convolution $(x*f)(g)=\int x(gy)f(y)\,dy$ is again such a cuspidal member, and the classes of $x$ and of $x*f$ in the cuspidal subcarrier, the closed subspace of the weighted $L^2$ space on $\Phi_0$ generated by cuspidal members, differ in norm by less than $\varepsilon$.
--
--   This is the statement that level-spherical, flat-symmetric archimedean smoothing functions act as approximate identities on cuspidal classes in the weighted $L^2$ space of a slab fundamental domain, here for the principal congruence level $K(N)$ rather than the level-one family used in the pins defining the space of members. It is used in the finite eigen-decomposition of isotypic cusp forms, where it bounds the part of a class annihilated by the smoothing operator.
